{
  "area": "discovery",
  "description": "AGSC-06-41 as amended 2026-11-10, the successor of disc-0027. The Dataset block of the home page is the node `@id` `site.base` (the Bundle IRI), so that its triples describe the Bundle and do not float on a blank node; its `creator` Person has the `@id` of its ORCID iD URL, or `<site.base>#creator` when no iD is configured, and `prov:wasAttributedTo` names that Person by `@id`, so a JSON-LD reader finds one Person and not two. Cases `configured`, `nothing-configured` and `restricted` are those of disc-0027 with these changes; `creator-without-orcid` names the Person by the fragment. With `discovery.dcat` set to `true` (`dcat-catalogue`), the page carries, beside the Dataset block, a DCAT 3 catalogue block (W3C Recommendation, 22 August 2024): a `dcat:Catalog` `<site.base>#catalog` whose `dcat:dataset` is the Bundle IRI as a `dcat:Dataset` with `dcterms:title`, `dcterms:description`, `dcterms:license`, `dcterms:creator`, `dcterms:modified` (the build instant) and one `dcat:Distribution` for each `DataDownload` of the Dataset block, with `dcat:downloadURL` and `dcat:mediaType` the IANA media type IRI of the served type, or `dcterms:format` for the chunks, whose type is not registered; `catalog` is null when the switch is off. Each block is compared as a JSON value. Derived by hand from the rule.",
